+// wwe2k14 patch (Session 7, PROTECT): every upload to GPU shared memory and every resolve watch their
+// pages for guest writes (SharedMemory::MakeRangeValid -> PhysicalHeap::EnableAccessCallbacks in all three
+// physical views), ~2-4% of the command processor thread in heavy WWE 2K14 entrance frames (stacks_111:
+// VirtualProtect ~70% of it, the per-page loop and the global critical region most of the rest). Pages
+// already watched are skipped by the original loop (the watch bit means "write-protected"), so only
+// unwatched pages are ever protected; what is left to save is the number of VirtualProtect calls and the
+// loop. Defined here (rexruntime) and read by the GPU plugin through REXCVAR_DECLARE.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gpu_protect_batch, false, "GPU",
+                    "Physical memory write watches with fewer VirtualProtect calls and less looping: "
+                    "one call per run of newly watched pages joined over up to 64 already watched, "
+                    "committed, guest-writable pages (normally read-only already), the same when "
+                    "access violations make pages writable again (joined over unwatched, committed, "
+                    "guest-writable pages, normally writable already), watched pages passed over by "
+                    "bit scan without reading the page table, and one entry into the global critical "
+                    "region per SharedMemory::MakeRangeValid. Same pages watched and unwatched. Final "
+                    "host protection also the same, except on joined pages the original code left "
+                    "inconsistent (a watched page made writable again without unwatching it: made "
+                    "read-only again here, so its next guest write invalidates - an extra invalidation "
+                    "at most, never a lost one) or that a guest allocation/protection change on another "
+                    "thread is changing at that moment. No joining while protect_on_release is on. "
+                    "Read per call (toggle-safe)");
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gpu_protect_batch_verify, false, "GPU",
+                    "With gpu_protect_batch: query the host protection (VirtualQuery) of every joined "
+                    "gap before and of every protected or unprotected range after the call (expected "
+                    "read-only when watching, read-write when unwatching), and recompute which pages "
+                    "the original loop would have watched; count and log mismatches ([s7][PROTECT], "
+                    "slow). Joined gaps not already at the target protection (stale watches the original "
+                    "code left, see gpu_protect_batch) are counted and logged separately as gap changes, "
+                    "not as mismatches");
